Z||000011||pherder||09-18-2000||06:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIEROCIOUS:<BR><B>Centerforce could care less whos money they take be it Archie or Bostitch's!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They do if they have an exclusive contract with Archie ... lawyers get involved then.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>The clutch will fit any of the 2.8 GM cars so it can be sold (and is sold) to anyone.  It would be interesting to see if Centerforce <B>WOULD</B> sell those part numbers to anyone (or if someone like JEGS/Summit can order that part number!)<P>Paul <BR>88 Coupe w/93 HO Quad 4, 97 Isuzu 5 speed and a Centerforce dual friction clutch!  (only the throwout bearing is different!)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||fsrowsell||09-18-2000||08:17 PM||||Hi HarryG, I took the Clutch disk, preasure plate and the flywheel to a machine shop. They centered it for me and taped the bolt holes for a cost of $30.00. The adapter plate is 1" steel. I bought my Centerforce from JEGS, the part number DF201914. The guy I was talking to was familiar with V8 Fiero's. It is a special order, So you have to wait 3 weeks or so. It's cheaper then Archie's...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Archie||09-18-2000||11:35 PM||||Well, I think it's about time I put in my two cents worth on all this.<P>Someone commented "Centerforce could care less whos money they take be it Archie or Bostitch's!" and someone else commented about lawyers. I would submit to you that CForce does care where the money comes from. In the last 2 years CF has sold a total of 176 of these F/W's. I bought 175 of them and ONE (1) was sold to someone else (with my approval) I would suggest that CForce would rather sell a hundred of these to me than ONE TO YOU. It is my design and I can pull my business out of CForce anytime.<P>In 1988 I had Bill Hays the owner and chief engineer of CenterForce design a custom Flywheel that had the features & profile I needed so it could be used with my V-8 Adapter system. During this developement I paid Centerforce several thousand $, for the prototyping and production of these F/W's. The agreement I had with Bill Hays was that these F/W's were unique and that, because of my payment of the developing costs, I was to be the sole distributor of them. Bill Hays retired about 5 years ago and turned the company over to his step son, Pat Wilson. So far, Pat has honored the previous agreement. A few years ago I saw the F/W's in the catalog but the sales people were not releasing them to other W/D's. <P>A V-8 Fiero Engine Conversion Kit is more than a Flywheel or an adapter plate. It is a group of parts that are specifically designed to work together and have been proven to work together under all circumstances for many years. A V-8 kit is not some rusty F/W bought from a junkyard & remachined, it's not some copy of a Zumwalt adapter plate manufactured in Michigan. <P>I'd like to address a couple of comments to a few other things I've seen posted in this thread but I'm trying to be nice. However, I am disappointed that a certain person would try to undermine my kit after all the help I've been to him in his assembly of a copy of one of my kits. I regret now that I helped you make that V-8 Archie COPY work in your car, I promise I won't be as helpful to the next guy who needs the same help you got. BTW, you have our car advertized as having a V-8 Archie kit in it, maybe you think that the name will help you sell the car. But, you and I know that it's a copy of my kit and I'd appreciate it if you would remove that reference from your ad.<P>Several people have asked me if I would buy IRM &/or Ryane Motorsports to carry on the work of those companies. In light of this thread and a couple of others I've seen in the last week, I'd like someone to tell me why I should bother to put up my money to continue those names.<P>I would like to suggest some additional reading for those who want to know just how much work, thought, engineering and planning go into the unique products of IRM, Ryane & V8Archie & others. Read this to learn more <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/arch5.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/arch5.htm</A> <P>thank You<P>Archie<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||spike||09-19-2000||11:25 AM||||Archie, it is sad that people are stealing your idea and selling copies of your kit. You know it all comes down to one thing, MONEY. People tend to do unholy things when it comes to saving a buck or two without ever realizing the effect.<P>All made possible by this money hungry, greedy world we live in.  <P>Tks. Mike.||||reg||1
Z||000015||rprevo||09-19-2000||03:45 PM|||| Sad?<BR>So when is GM going to sue someone for<BR>putting tires on a car that are round?<BR>In everything we do in America it is about<BR>improvment! Right now I am working on getting original documents from a protected source<BR>at the GM Proving grounds on some of the<BR>Fiero V8 cars that were tested, Don't<BR>know if this really happened or not but my<BR>source says he can prove it, Just waiting.<BR>I havn't been on the forum for long but<BR>it seems like any time someone puts a V8<BR>in a Fiero it's all copied off of Archies!<BR>and Boo Hoo Hoo! I admit the steps that<BR>were taken by Archie were outstanding steps<BR>in creativity but move on man and accept that<BR>people are going to do what you did, You can't stop it! Start putting V8's in Neons<BR>or something!!!<P> Ray,<BR> V8 Fiero that is not an Archie kit!<BR>Not even a hole in my fender!<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000016||FIEROCIOUS||09-19-2000||05:26 PM||||Whoa, Man! Archie I would never try to influence someone to not use your "kit"! I do however, feel that shareing ones knowledge freely can only benifit the majority while helping the minority!<P>Archie, wether it be an Archie kit a Zumalt kit or farmer bobs kit.<BR>With you being the ONLY major company still supplying kits you will only benifit from more V8 Fieros storming the streets as awarness of what this kit can do, this is by far the best advertisement that can be had!<P>The days of the "Fiero V8 kit wars" are gone and over with! Other companys have moved on to other niche markets with you being the last of the great supplyers.<P>So in contrast you can either get upset and rage on about the people who ripped you off, or cater to the needs of those useing incomplete kits! <BR>Regardless if you like it or not NO MONEY is less than some money! (ie. parts sold individualy!)<BR>Trust me Archie, I've seen your posts in other threads and if I were you I would like to forget! <BR>The more insistant and bitter you become the further people will want to be from a Archie kit! <BR>I am saying this as a friend not to de face you as an individual and the quality of your kits i think can never be disfaced your contributions to the fiero community is worth more than all the money that all the companys have stolen from you! Rest easy my friend. <BR>If you make it they will come.||||reg||1
Z||000017||rockcrawl||09-19-2000||09:22 PM||||technical difficulties<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 09-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||rockcrawl||09-19-2000||09:22 PM||||Archie,<BR> You've gone and done it again! I know you think you are "the man" when it comes to V8 Fieros, and I'm sure you are all you claim to be. But, the fact remains that not everyone wants to buy your kit. There are a lot of people who would rather complete the swap without a "kit".  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>A V-8 Fiero Engine Conversion Kit is more than a Flywheel or an adapter plate.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE> well for many of us, that's all it takes, we can figure out the rest, just as you once did. Do you think we're idiots? You were not the first guy to put a V8 in a Fiero, and you won't be the last. You talk like your way is the only way or the best way, but it can be done very succesfully without your help. Bostitch obviously started this thread because he needed an alternative. If you don't want to help then don't, but we don't need to hear you crying. You have proven to me (again) that I don't ever want to do bussiness with you. You have a lot of supporters on-line (do you pay them?), but I have heard nothing good said about you or your products at various Fiero related events. You need to make some changes in your attitude.<P>That is all.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000019||Archie||09-19-2000||10:54 PM||||This is getting pretty interesting, it's obvious that neither one of you guys have ever come up with an original idea of your own, let alone an original idea that someone would buy. You claim that I'm Bitter or mean spirited or whatever, that's totally wrong. I AM the only game in town and NO ONE will ever match my experience and customer service in regards to V-8 Fiero kits, so I'm not worried about your little endeavors. I'm worried about people who are going to pi$$ away good money on bad information. Earlier in this thread I saw people passing out Flywheel information that wasn't totally correct. In another thread (some of the same people) direct readers to an adapter plate from Street Dreams, which is just a copy of Zumwalts adapter & not supported by a Flywheel. I am concerned that members would order an adapter from that place and try to order a F/W from CForce thinking that they have saved a few $$. THOSE PARTS WILL ABSOLUTELY NOT WORK TOGETHER!!!! My goal was to once again try to keep people from Pi$$ing their money away on some of the bad information you guys are passing out and to set the record straight on where I stand.  <BR> <BR>You think I should just sit back and watch people do their best to undermine my original method of putting a V-8 into a Fiero. The only people that would suggest that are people who have never originated an idea of their own.<P>Sure, the idea of a V-8 in a Fiero is not mine alone & is not mine originally. However the method and original parts of my design are mine.<P>You state that the V-8 wars are over, and I agree. Gary Zumwalt is gone. When the "V-8 Wars" were going on, there were 2 totally different and totally original V-8 kits on the market. The one known as the Zumwalt kit and mine. None of the parts of these kits were interchangable with the other kit. Looking at the parts that comprised these 2 kits, there was no doubt that they were 2 totally DIFFERENT and INDEPENDANT designs to accomplish the same goal. Both of these kits accomplished the same thing by putting a V-8 into a Fiero. Both sides had reasons to argue that their method was better (I think I won that arguement). But the point is, rp, that if you want to come up with your own mounting system to install a V-8 into a Fiero then make it your own, don't copy Zumwalts kit & call it your own. Or search for ways to copy my designs.<P>Anyone that would like to get into the V-8 Fiero Engine conversion kit business is welcome. You'll have to compete with me, but competition is good for the breed. Just don't try to compete with me using a copy of my or someone elses' kit, do your own work and make your own design. The designer of the Zumwalt kit and I managed to find 2 totally different methods of making the V-8 Fiero dream come true. I'll bet that there is yet one more INDEPENDANT, UNIQUE and ORIGINAL way to putting the V-8 into the Fiero & you're welcome to look for it, just don't look in my parts bin. Go copy Zumwalts parts he's not here to protect himself.<P>rprevo, you say "...it seems like any time someone puts a V8 in a Fiero it's all copied off of Archies! and Boo Hoo Hoo" I've never suggested that you copied my kit, from your descriptions etc. I'm sure that yours is derived from the Zumwalt kit and I could care less. In case you haven't been reading this thread completely, maybe you better read it again, you'll see that your comments are ignoring the content of the thread.  This thread so far has mostly consisted of people discussing how to copy my method of doing the job. People have exchanged part numbers, sources and other information that makes it clear that the goal would be to target and reproduce items and parts that are unique to my method of doing a V-8 Fiero.  <P>As I've said before, my V-8 Conversion kit is more than a Flywheel or an adapter plate. It is a group of parts that are specifically designed to work together and have been proven to work together under all circumstances for many years and includes the proper customer support for that kit.<P>I am proud to stand up and protect the items that make up my original design. If you want to call me names, then go ahead. But before you tell me that I should just turn the other cheek, think about how you would react if someone did the same to something you originated.<P>Don't mistake my comments as bitter or mean or anything other than constructive corrections. <P>I see that rockcrawl has put in his 2 cents worth by making more personal comments but no  factual comments. <P>He states about flywheels and adapter plates.... "well for many of us, that's all it takes, we can figure out the rest, just as you once did. Do you think we're idiots?"<P>First off Jon, If someone gives you the adapter plate and the F/W, then you would have to be an Idiot not to be able to figure it out from there.<P>I think everything else in Jon's post has been addressed above.<P>Now, take another look at this thread, it wasn't about an alternate V-8 kit.... From the very first post it was about copying my kit.  In the first post BOSTITCH stated "Well basically I can't afford archie's kit so I need to find alternate source for the bell housing adapter piece and flywheel"  <P>fsrowsell, FIEROCIOUS, rprevo & rockcrawl, maybe you guys should actually read the threads you are responding to, before you take off flaming me. <P>Archie ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Terrybogin||09-19-2000||11:17 PM||||I was wondering how long it would take you to get here Archie! Before anything is said about my thread on the super cheap adapter plate- I was thinking about one for the 3.8 v6- not a v8. Now I understand that I dont need an adapter for that engine. So- please carry on the pi$$ing match without me.||||reg||1
Z||000021||FIEROCIOUS||09-20-2000||12:14 AM||||Well, a little more piss to the puddle! LOL<P>Um Archie, I know Bostitch I know that he got his name for the forum from a stapler on his desk cause he couldn't come up with a name! I also know that he is NOT putting a V8 into his Fiero that in fact he is putting a 4.3 into it! Fact is he needs a 4.3 kit! Do you sell one?<BR>Hmm no what do you say, you would have to modify it? hmmm seems like you could make your own kit for the same effort?<P>I am actualy doing the same 4.3 because it is ILLEGAL to put a V8 into a car that was never produced with a V8 option! That is going by the federal guidelines for engine swaps.<BR>I could give two shits for law but it is a consideration! Yes I would do unholy things to avoid a $5,000.00 fine aka (money)<P>Archie you claim that I have not been paying attention? What I have paid attention to is that you are never willing to help others unless it benifits you in some way.<P>Why couldn't you share your information about F/W at the begining of the thread instead of all this political bullshiz?<P>I would love to be as enlightened as you on V8 Fieros! If I have any knowledge of any subject that could help another person you bet I will share it matter of factly if someone asked me who to get a V8 kit from I would send them your way in a heartbeat!  <P>While being a little esentric you know your stuff and that is what counts!  <P>Archie truth be told if a V8 Fiero was never invented by you or Zummalt someone else would have done it. <P>If I were to come up with the kit, it would probably take me a year to get it right then someone else would want one too then more then I would say to myself, "Hey I can make money doing this!" I would start my own company doing something I love (Fieros) and make money at the same time! But wait isn't that what you did? You originaly started this whole thing for what? Money or fun?<BR>I don't ever plan to make a kit or any money off of V8 Fieros all I want is a unique Fiero that is fast as hell! <P>Maybe just maybe there wouldn't be so many Fiero engine swap types if V8 Fieros were more economicaly and politicaly frustrating?<P>Seems it would be alot easier to buy a "kit" then to make up an engine swap of another engine? Lets see to date that I know of we have  (2.2) (2.5) (Quad4) (super duty 4) (2.8) (3.1) (3.3) (3.4) (3800) (3800SC) (N*)<BR>(Caddy 4.9) (Caddy 500) (SBC) Just to name a few! Seems if it was so easy to do a "kit" people would be rushing out to get a V8 into their Fiero! But they are not why? I ask you Archie why? Why would a person choose a harder more expensive swap over one that is easier and cost less money? <BR>I will tell you that I was seriously contemplateing a Northstar just because I didn't want to deal with a V8 Fiero "kit"<P>I still don't! <BR>Sad thing is, if and only if, I have no other options I will be forced to buy a V8 Archie kit!<BR>But that is what Archie wants us the consumer to be FORCED to buy his kit!<P>Monopoly's suck and only make the "breed" imbreed! <p>[This message has been edited by FIEROCIOUS (edited 09-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||V8Fiero||09-20-2000||12:18 AM||||WOW! This is pretty intense. I will make my point brief. I, like many in this forum, have only enough money to scape by. I wanted to do the V8 swap in my car. I just couldnt see trying to "rig" up some sort of "makeshift" kit to put in the v8. <P>1. Why would I want to spend x amount of dollars on something that I have no clue if its going to work,<P>2. I really dont want something untested and unproven one foot behind my head doing 90 mph on the highway.<P>Just my thoughts.<BR>Thanks.||||reg||1
