Z||000025||fiero56||09-20-2000||08:52 AM||||Notice that Archie says free <B>customer</B> service. Not, "free service for farmer Bob and his neighbor". <BR>Archie has every right to ignore anyone looking for info on how to re-create his kits. I know of many businesses that will do nothing for you if you are not a customer of theirs. I work for a place like this. If you bring something in, and didn't buy it from us, forget about service, we won't do a damn thing. But, if you buy a product of ours, we will give you customer service and more product support than anyone can handle. And we do it all for free as long as you bought it from us.<P>The v-8 engine illegal thing. I wonder how Archie or Zumwalt could have even run a business if that were the case. <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||Zorba||09-20-2000||12:21 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by BOSTITCH:<BR>[B]Well basically I can't afford archie's kit  <P>Wow. Talking about intense...Here's my opinion in case anyone cares:<P>1. Archie has the right to defend his product. (:<P>2. I would not use the word monopoly. I think he has succeeded where his competition has failed. (; He also posts how to install his kit into your car on his web site. This demonstrates he is sharing his knowledge.<P>3. I believe Archie- if you read this - that he will gladly sell individual parts of your kit, including the flywheel. Please correct me if I am wrong here.<P>4. I have purchased his 200mph speedo for a car that had a Zumalt Kit. I am sure you can purchase his 4-core radiator, flywheel, adaptor plate, etc. separately.<P>5. He doesn't want you copying his stuff anymore then you would, if it were your own. But he's suspicious of any individual part purchases. I for one, need a flywheel from him in case a friend sells me he's unused kit. So, if someone sells you an unused kit where the flyhwheel was sold to someone else, will Archie NOT sell you the missing parts to complete your conversion. I highly doubt it.<P>6. I don't think Archie has claimed to be the only game in town but he CAN make a claim as to his "experience" and "know-how".<P>7. Archie doesn't work for free and sharing his expertise can cost him money.<P>8. I think he has been burned a few times and thus his attitude. We all get that way.<P>9. Archie, I think you need to clarify what you will and will not do as far as selling individual parts of your kit for the minority who genuinely may need them to complete a conversion with a used "original" kit.<P>10. Business is business and everyone is in business to make money and watch for themselves and what's best for them. The days of sharing, being nice and friendly are over. I am always puzzled and shocked when someone does something nice to me for "nothing" and lately I have run into such people. Which makes me want to be nice in return.<P>IF you can afford $950, buy his kit and you won't have to be outsourcing anything. However, if you have access to a used original kit (original, I said)...see if archie will sell you the parts you are missing. I think he will. <P>I also think that there are more v8 fieros on the road thanks to archie's kit than any other, whether they be more practical or not.<P>Just my thoughts on this whole debate.||||reg||1
Z||000027||FIEROCIOUS||09-20-2000||01:26 PM||||First off after looking at my previous threads I noticed I got a bit off subject in my rant! <P>I am not against V8 Archies kit or any of Archies products.<P>I would however like to buy pieces individualy and install a 4.3<P>I don't like to be told what I can and can't do for the benifite of others ie. (Told I can't install this engine on my own because I would be copying someone?) F off realy!<P>Trust me I will not copy Archies or Zumalts cause I think they both can be improved.<P>However, I still need an adapter plate and a flywheel and I can't get around that! So I guess I am guilty of copying you Archie Ha Ha. Whatever!<P>In reply to customer service I belive that if you share info to all not just your customers those who are not your customers soon will be! Why because you shared your knowledge and people honestly do want more than a product they want assurance and knowledge in this respect that is why Archie won the V8 wars! Now I am simply giveing my opinion on how I would catter to others needs.<BR>How much time out of your day does it realy take to help others? About the same amount of time it is takeing me to write this for Bostitch!<BR>Archie you claim to know me? Tell me and the rest of the forum members a bit about me! Hummor me please!<BR>One things for sure I can't spell for a d@mn!<P>A V8 in a Fiero is illegal in my state Utah and the federal guidelines suggest that other states follow suit.<P>If you have the new IM 240 machines (if you don't now you will soon) It actualy ask how many cylinders you have! Now the tricky part, the testing equipment only gives you options that your car was originaly available with that is 4 or 6 cylinders for a Fiero.<P>So if you have a V8 no matter how clean it runs even if it emmited pure oxygen from the tail pipe it would fail the visual inspection and due to it's increased displacement the equipment would not register properly. Even Billy Bob redtech can tell the differance between a V8 and a 2.8 V6!<P>Trust me I would rather install a Northstar than the 4.3 but If I want to pass the visual and emissions test I alas can't!<P>Thanks for the space <P>||||reg||1
Z||000028||mshill||09-20-2000||02:52 PM||||fierocious,  I am hoping that eventualy California will get rid of the visual inspection process.  Why can't they just stick that thing in the tailpipe and if it's clean, who cares if there's a jet engine in there.  ||||reg||1
Z||000029||rprevo||09-20-2000||03:51 PM|||| It amazes me how this allways turns out this<BR>way, I still think it's time for you to reinvest in some new projects Archie, I didnt<BR>copy I improved, I don't use your plate I don't use your upside down water pump and<BR>I had many Michigan performance shops oppinions on what to do with the flywheel<BR>and I am not interested in making any money<BR>off of a v8 Fiero kit I only get tired of<BR>insecure people that need to move on. I enjoy<BR>seeing people with enough creativity to finish there projects. If you have sold as many kits as you claim you should reduce your<BR>price cause I can have 6 adapter plates made<BR>for 125.00 a piece. If you have your flywheel<BR>inspected for cracks your know safer then<BR>with a stock one, Any one that dosn't do<BR>something to improve there firewall after<BR>a conversion like this shouldn't attempt a conversion. I really think other companys<BR>made there money and moved on I don't think they were eliminated just better investers.<BR>There were no Fieros harmed in the making<BR>of this post.<P> Ray<BR>Slam away pal||||reg||6
